  "notes": "USAGE:\nA cooking term commonly found in recipes. The {素|す} prefix means \"plain\" or \"without additions,\" contrasting with {天|てん}ぷら (tempura, battered and fried) or {唐揚|からあ}げ (coated with starch or flour). Commonly used for vegetables like {茄子|なす} (eggplant), {蓮根|れんこん} (lotus root), and {南瓜|かぼちゃ} (pumpkin).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {素揚|すあ}げにする (to deep-fry without coating)\n- {素揚|すあ}げした{野菜|やさい} (vegetables fried without batter)\n- {素揚|すあ}げにして{塩|しお}で{食|た}べる (to deep-fry plain and eat with salt)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {天|てん}ぷら: tempura — battered and deep-fried\n- {唐揚|からあ}げ: deep-fried with starch coating — typically for chicken",
